/S /H3
/P 46 0 R
/T (F. Kangaroos are mainly herbivores. They eat grasses, flowers, leaves, ferns, moss, and even insects. Like cows, kangaroos bring their swallowed food up again to the mouth and re-chew it before it is ready to be totally digested. Great kangaroos mainly roam forests in search of food, though they do go to open grasslands for grazing. Small species, like rat-kangaroos, eat worms, roots, and palm berries. The animal sits on its haunches while eating and finds food by digging. They are solitary, but have been seen feeding together.)
/E (F. Kangaroos are mainly herbivores. They eat grasses, flowers, leaves, ferns, moss, and even insects. Like cows, kangaroos bring their swallowed food up again to the mouth and re-chew it before it is ready to be totally digested. Great kangaroos mainly roam forests in search of food, though they do go to open grasslands for grazing. Small species, like rat-kangaroos, eat worms, roots, and palm berries. The animal sits on its haunches while eating and finds food by digging. They are solitary, but have been seen feeding together.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
