/Title (C. Probably the best-known fact about kangaroos is that they carry their young in a pouch. A female kangaroo can give birth to up to four offspring at one time, though this is unusual. At birth, the baby, called a joey, can be as small as a grain of rice. When the joey is born, it is guided safely into the comfy pouch, where it develops for another 4 to 15 months. Inside the pouch, the joey is protected and fed with milk. Joeys grow quickly, and at 14 to 20 months for females, or 2 to 4 years for males, they will be fully matured.)
